## 2. Custom 60-Second OTP Verification & Regeneration Flow
We will implement a custom verification route in `auth.py` that manages OTP generation, validation, and regeneration with a strict 60-second expiration.

```
                  [User requests OTP]
                           │
                           ▼
            Generate 6-digit OTP + Expiry (now + 60s)
                           │
                           ▼
                  [Verify within 60s?]
                   /             \
                 YES              NO
                 /                 \
     [Account Activated]      [OTP Expired -> Call /resend-otp]
```

### Proposed Changes:

#### [MODIFY] [auth.py](file:///c:/Users/manik/Downloads/Email%20Suit/backend/app/api/auth.py)
*   **OTP Expiry Duration:** Change OTP expiry in `register_request` and `login_request` from `10 minutes` to `60 seconds` (`timedelta(seconds=60)`).
*   **OTP Verification Checks:** Keep the comparison using `datetime.now(timezone.utc) > user.otp_expires_at` to strictly enforce the 60-second window.
*   **[NEW] `/resend-otp` Endpoint:**
    *   Accepts `{"email": "user@domain.com"}`.
    *   Generates a new 6-digit OTP.
    *   Sets a new expiration timestamp (60 seconds from now).
    *   Sends the new OTP via email and updates the database record.

